                <pb facs="0619" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg585"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1267.)</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    copies of telegrams from the Stamford Manufacturing Company, dated April 23, 25,
                    and a telegram sent by me to the same, also a copy of a note to the minister for
                    foreign affairs, April 24, regarding the expulsion of Greek subjects, also a
                    telegram from the Stamford Company, April 25, 1897.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>







